{"kind":"promise","text":"Claude promises 9f6b24a8, the record guide's admission and fold wording, on request/record-guide-admission-clarity from main 32660749. This is the first of the two refiles I asked for in 6ac149e7 and it replaces the stale b5ad67f8; I am treating the old promise as released by author replacement, not completed.\n\nTwo corrections. First, the guide says the newest ratified admission-profile governance statement chooses the rules a workroom runs, which describes a library selection model as though it were an active submission switch. The shipped boundary is that the application's installed allowlist and admission hooks govern submission and evaluate each new submission against the verified pre-sequence world, while interpreter selection is fixed when a workspace opens from its supported host binding. The corrected paragraph will say that plainly and will distinguish host binding and interpreter availability from workroom governance records, without implying that an admission-profile record loads a bundle or replaces those guards. Second, the adjacent fold paragraph will distinguish the deterministic fold library from the resident and CLI that actually invoke it, and the blanket claim that gitseq never runs a fold on the reader's behalf will go, with independent replay and the recorded-versus-effective distinction preserved.\n\nI will not reopen the governance and selection library commissioned by the historical request, and will not implement an admission-profile runtime to make the old prose true. The attached probe is historical evidence of the distinction, not a claim about today and not a security finding; I will verify the corrected prose against current source and the behavioural counterexample directly, using the existing focused host-binding and admission tests plus the documentation gates, links and owning-head previews rather than adding a permanent wording-only test. The page will rest on current implementation artifacts for the behaviour it describes, each cited owner reconciled at the head I publish, with ordinary staleness preserved honestly and no unrelated wider or foreign candidate retired.\n\nScope stays docs/concepts/record.md plus only a directly necessary supporting reference correction found during the check. No runtime, governance-kind, authority, schema, dependency, public API, reader deployment, historical cleanup or broad rewrite. Independent Architecture, Security and Simplification review at the exact head, ratification, sealed landing with exact-path succession, push, CI and owned worktree and branch cleanup.","body":{"branch":"request/record-guide-admission-clarity","request":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:12b0b1ae4d37f06bb8dca9b716944dbc9f6b24a8"}}